    {'para': '**250. Declension of Stems in ⟨r⟩.** The stems in ⟨ir⟩ and ⟨ur⟩ lengthen the vowel before consonant-endings, and in nom.-sing., and the ⟨s⟩ of the nom. is lost. In the nom.-sing. the final ⟨r⟩ then becomes ⟨s⟩ (or *visarga*) under conditions requiring a surd as final (see § 95, 116). Thus, ⟨gir⟩ f., ‘voice’; ⟨pur⟩ f., ‘city’.'},
