    {'para': '**252. Derivative stems in ⟨as⟩, ⟨is⟩, ⟨us⟩.** The stems of this division are mostly neuter; but there are a few masculines and feminines. Their inflection is nearly regular (for ⟨o⟩, ⟨ir⟩, ⟨ur⟩ before ⟨bh⟩ see § 241; for the loc. pl., p. 27, bottom of page). Masc. [and fem.] stems in ⟨as⟩ lengthen the ⟨a⟩ in nom. sing.; and the nom.-acc. pl. neut. also lengthen ⟨a⟩ or ⟨i⟩ or ⟨u⟩ before the inserted nasal (*anusvāra*). Thus, ⟨manas⟩ n., ‘mind’; ⟨havis⟩ n., ‘oblation’; ⟨dhanus⟩ n., ‘bow’.'},
